LEHU descends from FastCarPlay, a C++ CarPlay and Android Auto receiver:
  https://github.com/niellun/FastCarPlay  (Niellun and contributors, GPL-3.0)
  https://github.com/mbt28/FastCarPlay    (the F1C200s port, by LEHU's author)
Its designs for the protocols, the audio mixer, the video path and the
screens were carried over into Rust. The port's native CarPlay and Android
Auto backends were written after LIVI's, file by file, and LEHU's ports of
them keep that descent; the list below names the LIVI files.

LIVI, a Rust CarPlay and Android Auto host, Copyright (C) 2025 Lasse
Heitgres, GPL-3.0-or-later:
  https://github.com/f-io/LIVI
Files are named as they were when the code was taken: the TypeScript and
Python of its Electron era (src/main/services/projection/driver/, until
August 2026) and the Rust crates of its helper (native/livi-helperd/crates/)
since. Each LEHU file below says the same in its header. Everything was
rewritten in Rust and changed for LEHU.

CarPlay, crates/lehu-cp/src:
  av.rs, control.rs, info.rs: cp/stack/cpStack.ts, screenStream.ts,
    audioStream.ts, timingServer.ts, micUplink.ts, getInfo.ts;
    livi-cp/src/stack.rs, info.rs.
  pairing.rs: cp/stack/pairSetup.ts, pairVerify.ts, authSetup.ts,
    mfiSigner.ts, identity.ts, pairings.ts; livi-cp/src/pair_setup.rs.
  srp.rs: cp/stack/srp.ts.
  tlv8.rs: cp/stack/tlv8.ts; livi-cp/src/tlv8.rs.
  cipher.rs: cp/stack/controlCipher.ts; livi-cp/src/control_cipher.rs.
  crypto.rs: cp/stack/crypto.ts; livi-cp/src/crypto.rs (and its tests).
  plist.rs, the binary form: cp/stack/bplist.ts; livi-cp/src/bplist.rs.
  rtsp.rs: cp/stack/rtspMessage.ts.
  hid.rs, the report descriptors: cp/stack/hid.ts; livi-cp/src/hid.rs.
  nalu.rs, the configuration record detection: cp/stack/nalu.ts.
  iap2.rs: cp/iap2/link_layer.py; iap2-link.
  carplay_msg.rs, the identification and the route guidance display
    component: cp/iap2/control_session_message/*.py; bt/cp_handler.py.
  usbmux.rs: cp/iap2/muxd.py.
  media.rs: cp/iap2/control_session_message/now_playing.py and
    route_guidance.py; iap2-csm; the manoeuvre table of
    shared/utils/translateNavigation.ts.
  file.rs: cp/iap2/file_transfer.py and LIVI's file transfer receiver.
  mfi4.rs with mfi4/, opack.rs, vehicle.rs, ui_sync.rs, ultra.rs
    (CarPlay Ultra): livi-cp/src/mfi4/, opack.rs, vehicle_state.rs,
    ui_sync.rs, info.rs, stack.rs: the MFi 4 mutual authentication (its
    message and parameter ids, the SIGMA-I key derivation and channels,
    the compressed certificate layout and the DER rebuilt from it, the
    tunneled pair-setup and the pair-verify binding), the OPACK codec,
    the vehicle state protocol and its route sharing accessory, the UI
    sync messages, the display panel carrying the plug-in, the start and
    identification parameters. The key material and certificate tests
    use values computed with LIVI's code.
  scripts/ultra-theme.py: livi-core/src/theme_catalog.rs.
Most of these reached LEHU through FastCarPlay's src/protocol/cp, whose
files name the LIVI file each mirrors.

Android Auto, crates/lehu-aa/src:
  aoap.rs, the switch: livi-aa/src/usb.rs.
  transport.rs, opening the accessory's pipe: livi-session-io/src/usb.rs.
  proto.rs: ping_config from livi-aa/src/session.rs; the message
    definitions are LIVI's aap_protobuf (later livi-aa-proto), vendored by
    FastCarPlay.
  aaw.rs: the wireless setup definitions of aap_protobuf/aaw (later
    wireless_setup.proto).
  status.rs: livi-aa-stack/src/channels/media_info.rs, navigation.rs,
    nav_maneuver.rs.
  frame.rs: the frame flag classes of aa/stack/constants.ts, through
    FastCarPlay's aa_const.h.
The rest of the crate is a port of FastCarPlay's src/protocol/aa.

Elsewhere:
  lehu/src/host.rs, the Linked Phones ordering, and the presence states
    of crates/lehu-core/src/devices.rs: livi-core/src/devices.rs,
    livi-core-proto/src/state.rs.
  Device arbitration and several protocol behaviours (the 5 s TCP
    keepalive, the exit-button answer, a superseded session) follow
    LIVI's as behaviour, not code.

aasdk, Copyright (C) 2018 f1x.studio (Michal Szwaj), GPL-3.0-or-later:
  https://github.com/f1xpl/aasdk
The Android Auto (GAL) protocol as aasdk reverse engineered it: the
message ids and the protobuf field numbers of the messages the head unit
uses (through LIVI's definitions and FastCarPlay), and the head-unit
client certificate and key in crates/lehu-aa/src/cert.rs, which aasdk
published (src/Messenger/Cryptor.cpp) and phones accept.

In LIVI's tree but not LIVI's: crates/lehu-video/csrc/decoder.c,
crates/lehu-drm/src/display.rs and crates/lehu-input/src/evdev.rs share
code with native/livi-ui/app/src/kms/ on LIVI's F1C200s branch, which
LEHU's author wrote and contributed there (ported from FastCarPlay's
V4l2DrmDecoder and camera); so does the fontique change below.

vendor/fontique is fontique 0.11.1 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT, the Linebender
project) with two changes, marked in the files: the collection's version
counter cast for targets without 64-bit atomics, and a generic family
fontconfig cannot match left empty. vendor/parley is parley 0.11.1
(Apache-2.0 OR MIT, the Linebender project) with its dictionary
segmenters left out to spare 3 MB of tables. vendor/README.md describes
both.

The screens embed Open Sans Regular 3.003, Copyright 2020 The Open Sans
Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/opensans), licensed under
the SIL Open Font License 1.1: crates/lehu-ui/ui/fonts/OFL.txt. Its
